From 129ec6241c10fb5a671a42b0174d04e637e6a77a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:53:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] tla: model hup's conf change check and maybeAppend's
 atomic commit

Two rules in the code that election safety depends on across config
changes, which the spec did not model:

- raft.go hup refuses to campaign while there are committed but unapplied
  conf changes (hasUnappliedConfChanges). Timeout now requires that every
  committed config entry has been applied.
- handleAppendEntries appends, commits up to min(m.Commit, last new index)
  and replies with the last new index in one step (raftLog.maybeAppend).
  The spec appended in NoConflictAppendEntriesRequest and committed and
  replied in a later AppendEntriesAlreadyDone step, so a follower could
  hold new config entries without knowing that the previous config entry
  had committed.

Without both, a 71-step behavior within MCetcdraft's bounds elects two
leaders in one term: from config {1,2,3}, add 4 then remove 3; node 3 has
both entries but does not know the first committed, and campaigns on the
old config with {1,3} while another node wins on the new config.

Conflicting entries are still truncated one per step
(ConflictAppendEntriesRequest), as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tla/etcdraft.tla | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tla/etcdraft.tla b/tla/etcdraft.tla
index 87708b2..c6d83d4 100644
--- a/tla/etcdraft.tla
+++ b/tla/etcdraft.tla
@@ -316,6 +316,9 @@ CanProposeConf(i) ==
 \* @type: Int => Bool;
 Timeout(i) == /\ state[i] \in {Follower, Candidate}
               /\ i \in GetConfig(i)
+              \* raft.go hup: no campaign with committed but unapplied conf
+              \* changes (hasUnappliedConfChanges).
+              /\ ~HasUnappliedCommittedConfig(i)
               /\ state' = [state EXCEPT ![i] = Candidate]
               /\ currentTerm' = [currentTerm EXCEPT ![i] = currentTerm[i] + 1]
               /\ votedFor' = [votedFor EXCEPT ![i] = i]
@@ -629,7 +632,19 @@ NoConflictAppendEntriesRequest(i, index, m) ==
     /\ index > commitIndex[i]
     /\ HasNoConflict(i, index, m.mentries)
     /\ log' = [log EXCEPT ![i] = @ \o SubSeq(m.mentries, Len(@)-index+2, Len(m.mentries))]
-    /\ UNCHANGED <<messageVars, serverVars, commitIndex, durableState>>
+    \* raft.go handleAppendEntries: raftLog.maybeAppend appends the entries
+    \* and commits up to min(m.Commit, last new index) in the same step, and
+    \* the reply carries the last new index (MsgAppResp{Index: lastnewi}).
+    /\ CommitTo(i, Min({m.mcommitIndex, m.mprevLogIndex + Len(m.mentries)}))
+    /\ Reply([mtype           |-> AppendEntriesResponse,
+              msubtype        |-> m.msubtype,
+              mterm           |-> currentTerm[i],
+              msuccess        |-> TRUE,
+              mmatchIndex     |-> m.mprevLogIndex + Len(m.mentries),
+              msource         |-> i,
+              mdest           |-> m.msource],
+              m)
+    /\ UNCHANGED <<serverVars, durableState>>
 
 \* @type: (Int, Int, Bool, AEREQT) => Bool;
 AcceptAppendEntriesRequest(i, j, logOk, m) ==
